- op: discuss  # d959
  at: '2026-08-07T20:21:39Z'  # d959
  by: agent  # d959
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d959
  clock: 6  # d959
  nonce: d959  # d959
  message: "DONE by PR #246 (dev 5373b056c4), on behavioral evidence.\n\nShapes re-run on the merged tree:\n  def h(p: pathlib.Path, x): p.write_text(x)   external -> pathlib.Path,  tagged 0 -> 1\n  from pathlib import Path; def h(p: Path, x)  external -> pathlib.Path,  tagged 0 -> 1\n  import pathlib as pl; def h(p: pl.Path, x)   alias expands to pathlib.Path\n  def h(s: socket.socket, b): s.send(b)        external -> socket.socket, tagged 0 -> 1\n  AnnAssign and return-annotated factory       stay external, tagged 0 (deliberate)\n\nCORPUS: poetry 38 -> 52 reported boundaries (+14, +36.8%), sqlalchemy 43 -> 47\n(+9.3%). Additions are pathlib.Path.{exists,is_dir,is_file,stat,glob,iterdir,\nmkdir} on annotated parameters. Three adjudicated against source, all TRUE\nPOSITIVES (e.g. poetry \ncalling path.exists() and path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)).\n\nSCOPE WIDER THAN THIS ITEM WAS FILED FOR: the filing named the section 4 summary\nlookup (callees_at) as the blocked consumer. The io-boundary consumer was\nblocked too, by the same missing module slot. Both are unblocked.\n\nSCOPED TO PARAMETERS on measurement: of 95,245 external-placeholder method\nedges, 4,160 have a receiver with a resolvable annotation and 63 reach the\ncatalogue; 96% of that payload is the annotated-parameter shape. AnnAssign,\nreturn-annotated factories, attribute reads and generics contribute exactly\nzero and are pinned as excluded by tests that say why.\n\nDIRECTION: this ADDS classifications -- the first change in this area that does.\nSafety is the binding check, not the gate: a minted hint bypasses\ngate_named_entry and ambiguous_names by design (gating the hinted path costs\n61.5-87.2% of all boundaries, see INV-kipor). Raw annotation text was measured\nto produce CONFIRMED false boundaries (conn: Connection -> sqlite3.Connection.\nexecute plus a database-zone taint sink; 174 such annotations in the corpus).\nResolution reuses _import_binding_for from INV-kipor / PR #244.\n\nGO: nothing built, and that is measured. Go has no equivalent gap (96.7% of\npackage-qualified receivers already reach a usable module slot). Its residual\ninitializer-inference gap and the reason the obvious fix is net-harmful (17.1%\nwrong-symbol hijack rate for +0.61% gain) are filed as WI-kamin.\n\nDOES NOT CLOSE INV-linub. This is one instance (python, annotated parameters).\nStill open under that class: unannotated receivers, self.<field>.<method>()\nwhich emits NO call edge at all, kotlin (WI-nasuf), and the FP channels\nINV-fokik / INV-fazim.\n\nCOLD START, disclosed: 17 of the 18 catalogue entries this activates fire zero\ntimes on the corpus today, so their boundary labels have never been validated\nagainst real output. Path.{exists,is_dir,is_file,stat} are catalogued fs_read\nthough they stat rather than read contents -- a catalogue-labelling question,\nuntouched here. Relative imports, importlib, conditional and TYPE_CHECKING\nimports are unprobed. The 63-site population is a property of the six-repo bag:\nadding one repo moved it +20.6%."  # d959
- op: discuss  # ca9c
  at: '2026-08-07T20:22:17Z'  # ca9c
  by: agent  # ca9c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ca9c
  clock: 7  # ca9c
  nonce: ca9c  # ca9c
  message: "Correction to the previous entry: one line was truncated by shell quoting. The\nadjudicated example reads in full --\n\n  poetry src/poetry/utils/helpers.py:273-285\n\n      def is_dir_writable(path: Path, create: bool = False) -> bool:\n          try:\n              if not path.exists():\n                  if not create:\n                      return False\n                  path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n  path.exists() -> pathlib.Path.exists / fs_read\n  path.mkdir()  -> pathlib.Path.mkdir  / fs_write\n\nBoth are real filesystem operations on an annotated parameter, invisible before\nPR #246. The other two adjudicated sites:\n\n  src/poetry/utils/cache.py:334-340\n      def _get_cached_archives(self, cache_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n          paths += cache_dir.glob(...)              -> Path.glob / fs_read\n\n  src/poetry/inspection/info.py:472-483\n      def from_sdist(cls, path: Path) -> PackageInfo:\n          if path.is_file():                        -> Path.is_file / fs_read\n\n3 of 3 true positives on direct source reading."  # ca9c
- op: discuss  # 5cea
  at: '2026-08-08T19:24:34Z'  # 5cea
  by: agent  # 5cea
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5cea
  clock: 8  # 5cea
  nonce: 5cea  # 5cea
  message: "FOLLOW-ON SHIPPED: PR #247 (dev e54a20c07e) — a derivation from a typed receiver\nkeeps the type, for an allowlisted member only.\n\n#246 typed the ROOT (annotated parameter). #247 keeps that type across a\nderivation, which is what makes the root typing pay:\n\n    p = d / \"f.txt\"        -> pathlib.Path   (was external)\n    p = d.joinpath(\"f\")    -> pathlib.Path   (was external)\n    tests = path / \"tests\"; tests / \"__init__.py\"   (recurses)\n\nMEASURED against a post-#246 baseline so the delta is attributable to #247\nalone: poetry 52 -> 57 (+5, all five TRUE POSITIVES read against source);\nsqlalchemy 47 -> 47 (+0, a real zero — a DB library barely derives paths).\nmitmproxy moved 248 -> 254 but its baseline PREDATES #246, so that +6 spans both\nchanges and is NOT credited to #247. Its sites are direct annotated-parameter\nuses (load_dhparam(path: Path) calling path.exists()/path.write_bytes()), i.e.\n#246's work. Recorded because the mislabel nearly reached a commit message.\n\nDEFAULT-DENY ALLOWLIST, measured: propagating by default is 25.9% precise (7/27\nadded boundaries) and mints 16 false taint sinks incl. 2 database + 2 network;\n85.1% of corpus hop>=1 propagations are provably wrong or unverifiable, 20 of\nthe 21 provably-wrong ones being a Path->str transition. Allowlist = 85.7%,\ncosts 3 boundaries of 427 (0.7%).\n\nNOT A NEW CATALOGUE. FileAnalysis.method_return_types (INV-dihos / WI-kuroj) is\nthe language-neutral return-type registry go.py and rust.py already populate;\npython populated it ZERO times. A proposed 9th YAML catalogue was refuted 3/3 on\nexactly this point. TYPE_PRESERVING_MEMBERS is the stdlib complement, same shape.\n\n=== RESIDUAL GAPS IN THIS FAMILY (none are regressions; all pre-existing) ===\n\n1. INLINE CHAIN ROOT emits NO CALL EDGE AT ALL:\n       (d / \"a\" / \"b.txt\").write_text(x)     -> zero edges, before AND after #247\n   The BOUND form works (p = d / \"a\" / \"b.txt\"; p.write_text(x)). This is the\n   attribute-chain-rooted-at-an-expression gap, not a typing gap — an EMISSION\n   defect upstream of everything here, and the same family as INV-mumov and the\n   `self.<field>.<method>()` hole. Sized: unmeasured.\n2. `.parent` / `.parents[n]` are ATTRIBUTE READS, a different AST shape; not\n   routed. Smaller population than the call/operator shapes.\n3. Path.cwd() / Path.home() — classmethods on the TYPE, not derivations.\n4. Interprocedural propagation (a derived Path returned from a helper): the\n   probe produced 0 edges; FP risk unmeasured.\n5. `for p in d.iterdir(): p.unlink()` loop targets: 0 boundaries in every mode.\n6. self.attr receivers: production does not type them either.\n\n=== INSTRUMENT FAILURES, recorded so the zeros are not read as absence ===\n\nKotlin and Swift populations for this family are NOT MEASURED — both failed\ntheir POSITIVE CONTROL, so their zeros are instrument nulls:\n  - kotlin emits NO unresolved method-call edge for a method call on a receiver\n    at all (only bare callees), so all 181 method-kind kotlin catalogue entries\n    are currently unreachable. That is WI-nasuf's territory, independently\n    corroborated here.\n  - swift puts the receiver VARIABLE NAME in the module slot: a probe produced\n    `swift:fm:0-0:fileExists` for a `fm` local. A variable name in a module slot\n    is a defect in its own right — filed separately."  # 5cea
